SINA_SMART["term1-endocrine"] = {"lecture":"term1-endocrine","title":"Endocrine system terminology","mapStatus":"auto: generated by universal.py from the lecture summary and key points; not human-reviewed","los":[{"id":"term1-endocrine:e0","text":"Hormones: secreted by endocrine glands directly into the blood.","topic":"The big picture","sec":0,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"term1-endocrine:e1","text":"Homeostasis: home/o constant + -stasis control.","topic":"The big picture","sec":0,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"term1-endocrine:e2","text":"adren/o adrenal; gonad/o gonads (testic/o, ovari/o); pancreat/o islets; parathyroid/o; pineal/o; pituit/o; thym/o; thyr/o.","topic":"Glands and combining forms","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"term1-endocrine:e3","text":"Pituitary controls the other glands, driven by hypothalamic neurohormones.","topic":"Glands and combining forms","sec":1,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"term1-endocrine:e4","text":"ACTH → adrenal cortex; TSH → thyroid; GH (somatotropic) → growth.","topic":"Pituitary hormones","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"term1-endocrine:e5","text":"FSH, LH/ICSH → gonads (ovulation, sperm, testosterone).","topic":"Pituitary hormones","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"term1-endocrine:e6","text":"Prolactin (lactogenic) → milk; MSH → melanin.","topic":"Pituitary hormones","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"term1-endocrine:e7","text":"ADH (antidiuretic) → water retention; oxytocin → labour contractions, milk flow.","topic":"Pituitary hormones","sec":2,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"term1-endocrine:e8","text":"Melatonin → circadian sleep-wake cycle.","topic":"Other glands","sec":3,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"},{"id":"term1-endocrine:e9","text":"Glucagon raises, insulin lowers blood glucose.","topic":"Other glands","sec":3,"importance":"core","highYield":"insufficient-source"}],"vmap":{},"mlevel":{"1rojeco":"a","1yi0c6n":"a","1xf2ko":"a","dvf0da":"a","j8do9h":"a","19rn7jb":"a","1dhefbr":"a","fqnpta":"a","zic9p5":"a","tqx2kv":"a","u2uguz":"a","1yflcy6":"a","9fp616":"a","1q5rs4w":"a","qteta3":"a","1wannet":"a"},"mapCounts":{"verified":0,"auto":16,"ambiguous":0,"missing":0},"mrules":[],"items":[],"experimental":[],"status":{},"difficulty":{},"expl":{"term1-endocrine:e0":{"s":0,"u":["Hormones: secreted by endocrine glands directly into the blood.","The endocrine system produces hormones , chemical messengers secreted by endocrine glands directly into the bloodstream , which together maintain homeostasis (home/o constant + -stasis control): a constant internal environment.","Hormone levels are measured in blood or urine."],"dp":[]},"term1-endocrine:e1":{"s":0,"u":["Homeostasis: home/o constant + -stasis control.","The endocrine system produces hormones , chemical messengers secreted by endocrine glands directly into the bloodstream , which together maintain homeostasis (home/o constant + -stasis control): a constant internal environment."],"dp":[]},"term1-endocrine:e2":{"s":1,"u":["adren/o adrenal; gonad/o gonads (testic/o, ovari/o); pancreat/o islets; parathyroid/o; pineal/o; pituit/o; thym/o; thyr/o.","adren/o adrenal glands (electrolytes, metabolism, stress); gonad/o gonads: testic/o testicles (sperm), ovari/o ovaries (ova); pancreat/o pancreatic islets (blood sugar); parathyroid/o parathyroids (calcium); pineal/o pineal gland (sleep-wake cycle); pituit/o, pituitar/o pituitary (controls the other glands); thym/o thymus (immune reaction); thyr/o, thyroid/o thyroid (metabolism, growth, nervous activity)."],"dp":[]},"term1-endocrine:e3":{"s":1,"u":["Pituitary controls the other glands, driven by hypothalamic neurohormones.","adren/o adrenal glands (electrolytes, metabolism, stress); gonad/o gonads: testic/o testicles (sperm), ovari/o ovaries (ova); pancreat/o pancreatic islets (blood sugar); parathyroid/o parathyroids (calcium); pineal/o pineal gland (sleep-wake cycle); pituit/o, pituitar/o pituitary (controls the other glands); thym/o thymus (immune reaction); thyr/o, thyroid/o thyroid (metabolism, growth, nervous activity)."],"dp":[{"h":"Why the pituitary is called the master gland","t":"Most pituitary hormones end in -tropic (having an affinity for): each one targets another gland, such as the adrenal cortex (ACTH) or the thyroid (TSH). The pituitary itself answers to the hypothalamus, forming a chain that keeps hormone levels in balance. Reading the -tropic hormone names tells you exactly which gland each one drives. Source: the lecture's pituitary slides."}]},"term1-endocrine:e4":{"s":2,"u":["ACTH → adrenal cortex; TSH → thyroid; GH (somatotropic) → growth.","Anterior lobe : ACTH (adrenocorticotropic: adren/o + cortic/o cortex + trop change) stimulates the adrenal cortex; FSH stimulates oestrogen and ova growth, and sperm production; GH (somatotropic: somat/o body) regulates growth of bone, muscle and tissues; ICSH and LH stimulate ovulation in females and testosterone in males; prolactin (LTH, lactogenic) maintains milk secretion (lact/o milk, gen producing); MSH increases melanin and skin darkening (often in pregnancy); TSH stimulates the thyroid."],"dp":[]},"term1-endocrine:e5":{"s":2,"u":["FSH, LH/ICSH → gonads (ovulation, sperm, testosterone).","Anterior lobe : ACTH (adrenocorticotropic: adren/o + cortic/o cortex + trop change) stimulates the adrenal cortex; FSH stimulates oestrogen and ova growth, and sperm production; GH (somatotropic: somat/o body) regulates growth of bone, muscle and tissues; ICSH and LH stimulate ovulation in females and testosterone in males; prolactin (LTH, lactogenic) maintains milk secretion (lact/o milk, gen producing); MSH increases melanin and skin darkening (often in pregnancy); TSH stimulates the thyroid."],"dp":[]},"term1-endocrine:e6":{"s":2,"u":["Prolactin (lactogenic) → milk; MSH → melanin.","Anterior lobe : ACTH (adrenocorticotropic: adren/o + cortic/o cortex + trop change) stimulates the adrenal cortex; FSH stimulates oestrogen and ova growth, and sperm production; GH (somatotropic: somat/o body) regulates growth of bone, muscle and tissues; ICSH and LH stimulate ovulation in females and testosterone in males; prolactin (LTH, lactogenic) maintains milk secretion (lact/o milk, gen producing); MSH increases melanin and skin darkening (often in pregnancy); TSH stimulates the thyroid."],"dp":[]},"term1-endocrine:e7":{"s":2,"u":["ADH (antidiuretic) → water retention; oxytocin → labour contractions, milk flow.","Posterior lobe (stores hypothalamic hormones): ADH (antidiuretic) reduces water lost in urine and helps control blood pressure; oxytocin (oxy- swift + -tocin labour) stimulates uterine contractions and milk flow and controls postnatal bleeding (synthetic form: Pitocin)."],"dp":[{"h":"Why ADH is 'anti-diuretic'","t":"Diuresis means increased urine production. ADH works against it by making the kidneys return water to the bloodstream, which concentrates the urine and supports blood pressure. The name, built from anti- + diuretic, states the function directly. Source: the lecture's posterior lobe slide."}]},"term1-endocrine:e8":{"s":3,"u":["Melatonin → circadian sleep-wake cycle.","Pineal : melatonin regulates the sleep-wake portion of the circadian cycle (24-hour biological rhythm)."],"dp":[]},"term1-endocrine:e9":{"s":3,"u":["Glucagon raises, insulin lowers blood glucose.","Pancreatic islets : control glucose (blood sugar, the body's basic energy) with glucagon (raises it) and insulin (lowers it)."],"dp":[]}},"meta":{"1rojeco":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e0/recall/1"},"1yi0c6n":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e1/recall/1"},"1xf2ko":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e3/recall/1"},"dvf0da":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e3/recall/2"},"j8do9h":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e8/recall/1"},"19rn7jb":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e3/recall/3"},"1dhefbr":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e4/recall/1"},"fqnpta":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e0/recall/2"},"zic9p5":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e6/recall/1"},"tqx2kv":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e6/recall/2"},"u2uguz":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e7/recall/1"},"1yflcy6":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e7/recall/2"},"9fp616":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e7/recall/3"},"1q5rs4w":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e8/recall/2"},"qteta3":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e9/recall/1"},"1wannet":{"a":"recall","vg":"term1-endocrine:e0/recall/3"}},"explRev":"9b4370841056"};
